<?xml version='1.0' encoding='utf-8'?>
<graphml xmlns="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns http://graphml.graphdrawing.org/xmlns/1.0/graphml.xsd">
  <key id="d2" for="node" attr.name="source_id" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d1" for="node" attr.name="description" attr.type="string" />
  <key id="d0" for="node" attr.name="entity_type" attr.type="string" />
  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;371ST ENGINEER CONSTRUCTION BATTALION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"371st Engineer Construction Battalion was activated as a Special Service Regiment in February 1944 and later redesignated as a General Service Regiment. It was formed at Camp Ellis, Illinois, and trained in the United States before being shipped overseas during World War II."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;371ST INFANTRY REGIMENT (UNITED STATES)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"371st Infantry Regiment (United States) is a military unit that participated in World War I, as evidenced by its recognition and historical documentation."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREDDIE STOWERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Freddie Stowers is a notable figure associated with the 371st Infantry Regiment (United States), though specific details about his connection are not provided in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;371ST REGIMENT OF INFANTRY, U.S.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"371st Regiment of Infantry, U.S. is another name for the 371st Infantry Regiment (United States), used interchangeably in some references."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;371ST INFANTRY REGIMENT (EN)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"371st Infantry Regiment (en) is the English version of the regiment's name, highlighting its official designation."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;371ST INFANTRY REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"371st Infantry Regiment is a military unit that participated in various campaigns during World War I, including the New Hebrides, New Guinea, and the Bismarck Archipelago."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMERICAN EXPEDITIONARY FORCES ON THE WESTERN FRONT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"American Expeditionary Forces on the Western Front is the organization that the 371st Infantry Regiment was assigned to during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNITED STATES 371ST INFANTRY REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"United States 371st Infantry Regiment is a specific designation of the 371st Infantry Regiment, emphasizing its affiliation with the United States."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;U.S. 371ST INFANTRY REGIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"U.S. 371st Infantry Regiment is another way to refer to the 371st Infantry Regiment, highlighting its U.S. affiliation."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;371ST BOMBARDMENT SQUADRON (HEAVY)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) is a military unit that was reconstituted and served in various capacities, including as a B-29 Superfortress squadron and a B-47 Stratojet medium jet bomber squadron."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-29 SUPERFORTRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-29 Superfortress is a type of aircraft used by the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) for long-range bombardment operations."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MACDILL FIELD, FLORIDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MacDill Field, Florida is a location where the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) was based and later reactivated."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LINCOLN AIR FORCE BASE, NEBRASKA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lincoln Air Force Base, Nebraska is a location where the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) was deployed after moving from Okinawa."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OKINAWA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Okinawa is a location where the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) was deployed during the Korean War."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW HEBRIDES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New Hebrides is a location where the 371st Infantry Regiment operated during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEW GUINEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"New Guinea is a location where the 371st Infantry Regiment operated during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BISMARCK ARCHIPELAGO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bismarck Archipelago is a location where the 371st Infantry Regiment engaged in long-range bombardment operations during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WESTERN PACIFIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Western Pacific is a broader location where the 371st Infantry Regiment operated during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEYTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leyte is a location where the 371st Infantry Regiment operated during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LUZON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Luzon is a location where the 371st Infantry Regiment operated during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOUTHERN PHILIPPINES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Southern Philippines is a location where the 371st Infantry Regiment operated during World War I."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;371ST BOMBARDMENT SQUADRON (PROVISIONAL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"371st Bombardment Squadron (Provisional) is a provisional unit that existed briefly before being inactivated in 1974."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;U-TAPAO AB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"U-Tapao AB is a location where the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) was based as a B-52 squadron."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-52&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-52 is a type of aircraft used by the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Provisional) and (Heavy) for various operations."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-58&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-58 is a type of aircraft used by the 366th Bombardment Squadron, Medium, which was inactivated in 1970."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BUNKER HILL AFB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bunker Hill AFB is a location where the 366th Bombardment Squadron, Medium, was based as a B-58 squadron."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MCCOY AFB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"McCoy AFB is a location where the 367th Bombardment Squadron, Heavy, was based as a B-52C/D squadron."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MACDILL AFB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MacDill AFB is a location where several bomb squadrons were based, including the 368th and 369th Bombardment Squadrons, Medium, and the 370th Bombardment Squadron, Medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLATTSBURGH AFB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plattsburgh AFB is a location where the 373d Bombardment Squadron, Medium, was based as a B-47 squadron."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRATEGIC AIR COMMAND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strategic Air Command is the organization to which the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) was reassigned after its initial deployment."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTISUBMARINE WARFARE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antisubmarine Warfare is the primary mission of the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) during the Korean War."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OPERATION REFLEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Operation Reflex is a deployment operation carried out by the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) to North Africa."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOREAN WAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Korean War is the conflict during which the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) carried out combat operations over Korea."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OKINAWA DEPLOYMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Okinawa Deployment is the event where the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) was deployed to Okinawa during the Korean War."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LINCOLN AIR FORCE BASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lincoln Air Force Base is a location where the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) was based as a B-47 squadron."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOEING B-47 STRATOJET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Boeing B-47 Stratojet is a type of aircraft used by the 371st Bombardment Squadron (Heavy) as a medium jet bomber squadron."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;B-47&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"B-47 is a type of aircraft used by multiple bomb squadrons, including the 368th, 369th, 370th, and 371st Bombardment Squadrons, Medium, and the 372d Bombardment Squadron, Medium."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;365TH BOMBARDMENT SQUADRON (PROVISIONAL)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"365th Bombardment Squadron (Provisional) is a provisional unit that existed briefly before being inactivated in 1974."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;366TH BOMBARDMENT SQUADRON, MEDIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"366th Bombardment Squadron, Medium is a medium bomb squadron that was based at Bunker Hill AFB and used B-58 aircraft."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0335-e4e7a7733e22</data>
    </node>
  </graph>
